WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:03.135
Okay, welcome to<i> Real Time</i>
on CNN.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.670
We're here
with Democratic strategist,

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.573
and co-host of
the<i> Politics War Room</i> podcast,

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.508
James Carville.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.276
And host of<i> The Rubin Report</i>
on YouTube

00:00:10.342 --> 00:00:11.944
and Rumble, Dave Rubin.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.747
(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:17.117
Okay, here are the questions.
For Dave,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.085
"What did you think
of Elon Musk's trip to Israel?

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:22.322
Do you think he
no longer harbors antisemitic

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:23.956
and conspiratorial beliefs?"

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:25.858
Oh, well,
he never had antisemitic

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.794
or conspiratorial beliefs
in the first place.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.028
-But Elon Musk...
-BILL MAHER: Well.

00:00:29.094 --> 00:00:30.363
...is not an antisemite.

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:31.998
There are plenty of antisemites
out there.

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.999
You called a whole bunch
of them out during the show.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.435
I mean, Elon Musk going
to Israel was absolutely great.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.338
I think too many people now
don't believe anything they see.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.474
-But they do believe Elon Musk.
-BILL: Well--

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:42.809
So him going there and saying,

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.811
"I saw the 47 minutes
of footage."

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.478
He's wearing dog tags of--

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:47.647
You know,
from one of the families...

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.916
-Okay. Well, I mean, it could--
-...who lost their kids.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.251
There's a lot
of antisemites out there,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.785
but Elon Musk
is not one of them.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:56.356
-Okay, that may be true. I...
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.791
I mean-- I mean... (CHUCKLES)
...look, he's a hard guy

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.159
to follow all the time.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.428
-I've tried, and the one--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:01:02.494 --> 00:01:04.497
This thing did test my patience
with him,

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.899
because he may not be
an antisemite,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.001
but when someone tweets
what they tweeted...

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.369
-DAVE RUBIN: Right.
-...and he tweets,

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.171
"You have spoken
the actual truth."

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.306
It looks really antisemitic.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.478
-So-- I mean, come on.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.478
DAVE: I mean, I don't know--

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.347
I don't know how in the weeds
you wanna get on the comment.

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:22.882
But the comment was really--

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:23.950
BILL: We do.
What is the comment?

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.751
The comment
that he was responding to

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.820
was about
that there are left-wing,

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.355 line:0%
thought of
as "Jewish organizations,"

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.623 line:0%
like the ADL,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.192 line:0%
that are aiming their fire
the wrong way all the time.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.693 line:0%
So they're attacking him, right?

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.796 line:0%
As opposed to attacking
the people that they--

00:01:36.862 --> 00:01:38.898
-That are actually antisemites.
-BILL: No, I think--

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.299
Like the lefties that you
were talking about earlier.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.934
All right, my understanding
of it was that he was supporting

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.703
the idea that--

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.405
Well, you heard
when you mentioned it during--

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:46.639
You're exactly right.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:49.508
It was the greatest act
of Jew-washing I've ever seen.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.111
-(LAUGHS)
-After he said something
like that.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:53.446
(CHUCKLES, SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.014
Yeah, I've never heard
that term.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.349
Well, I mean, it's what--

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.317
-it's what you do
when you screw up...
-BILL: Yeah. Oh, I get it.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.085
...and you go, "All right,
all right. I'll say a thing"

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:01.453
I mean, come on.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.089
Look, I have no-- no idea.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.923 line:0%
The last thing I wanna do
is pick a fight with a guy

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.292 line:0%
worth a trillion dollars.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.362 line:0%
But that dude is weird, man.
I'm gonna tell you.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.997 line:0%
There's something weird
about that boy.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:14.400 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-BILL: Uh...

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:18.070
Uh, James, you famously said,
"It's the economy, stupid,

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:21.307
but voters seem to be responding
to positive economic news...

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.309
voters don't seem
to be responding

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.110
to positive economic news
in the polls.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:26.312
How do you explain this?"

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.680
Well, you know,

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.682
you got 60 percent
of the Republicans

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.584
that believe the Earth
is 6,000 years old.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.818
BILL: Oh,
that's not a good answer.

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:33.986
-But, if what--
-BILL: Come on.

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.522
I'm just thinking,
you say the polls, all right?

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.258
You-- Look,
we had 5.6 percent growth.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.994
All right? I-- By any record--

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.929
Now, if people don't feel it,

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:47.166
and I-- Look, I think
we should've made a change.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.802
I-- I-- You and I agree on that.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.038
And I don't know
how much of it is

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.507
is that they can't see
beyond the present.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:58.311
I mean, the cost of living
has hurt people.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.780
But you just can't look
at this economy

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.515
and go out and say,
"This is a bad economy."

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.383
(HESITATES) That's impossible.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.318
But that's not really what
you wanna tell the voters.

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:07.253
You can't run--

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.254
But I'm not running
for office, Bill.

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:12.658
I'm answering a question
on a television show.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.026
-If I wasn't--
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.461
Okay, but you're-- but you're--

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:17.363
The reason why you're on
a television show

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:19.164
is because you're
a known strategist.

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.966
So we're asking
for your strategy,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.269
and your strategy seems
to be to tell the voters,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.637
"You don't know
what you're talking about."

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.872
And I don't think
that's a good way

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.706
to get elected,
and I'm not a strategist.

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:29.509
I would not say that.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:32.511
-But you can't--
-You just said it to me.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.413
-(GUESTS CHUCKLE)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.115
DAVE: He's not running
for office.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.750
-I mean, look at the sweatshirt.
-I know, but people...

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.886
Here's what I think it is.
People--

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:40.887
The things that--

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.821
Like you can cite
the statistics.

00:03:42.888 --> 00:03:44.657
And yes,
inflation is going down.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:45.858
It's going
in the right direction.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.059
But the things that--

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.428
The things people buy every day
in this country.

00:03:49.561 --> 00:03:53.365
-Bullets, eggs--
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.367
-BILL: Gas.
-Ga-- Gas is down.

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.770
-Ga-- Not here.
-But, I--

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.739
Well, I'm just telling you,
the price of gas...

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.107
-BILL: Yes. Right.
-We produce more--

00:04:02.174 --> 00:04:03.943
We pump more oil

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.978
than we ever have in history.

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:09.782
Anywhere. We pump more oil
than Saudi Arabia.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.017
All right?
Just so you know that.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.718
But if you ask people,

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:15.254
you know, "Do you think
that the Democrats

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.255
and Biden has been--"

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.257
You know, "Oh, yeah,
of course he is, 100 percent."

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.326
(HESITATES) I can't--

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.595
The fact that people
believe something

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.229
doesn't make it a fact.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.732
There's a big story in
<i>The Wall Street Journal</i> today.

00:04:26.932 --> 00:04:30.469
The crime rate
has dropped significantly.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.105
Try to tell--
(HESITATES) Argue with someone.

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:37.510
But the crimes per 100,000,
I think, were 738,

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:40.345
and are down to 362
or something like that.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.117
You-- I gotta sit here and act
like I'm a factual klutz

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.319
because somebody
believes something

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.421
that's not true?

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.555
I don't buy that.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.490
Okay. Well, then we'll move on.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.825
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:56.162
-BILL: Um...
-(CHUCKLES)

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.462
Mike...

00:04:57.896 --> 00:05:00.633
-(LAUGHS)
-(BILL CHUCKLING)

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:05.805
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:08.407
So, uh, Mike Johnson,

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:10.676
he's from your home state
of Louisiana.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.678
-Oh, man.
-BILL: The Speaker of the House.
I read today,

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.380
he wrote a foreword in a book

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.716
that conscribes
to conspiracy theories

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.383
and homophobic insults.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.553
I thought, "Mike Johnson wrote
the foreword to the Bible?"

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:25.057
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-Uh...

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.627
Do you think Mike Johnson
can hold his party together,

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.529
now that he
has taken the mantle?

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.430
First of all,

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.165
I don't think
he can hold his party together.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.067
Second of, you're exactly right,

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.136 line:0%
Mike Johnson
and what he believes

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:39.171 line:0%
is one of the greatest threats

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.274 line:0%
we have today
to the United States.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.243 line:0%
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)
-But I promise you.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.545
I know these people.

00:05:46.645 --> 00:05:48.280
BILL: You're talking
about Christian nationalism.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.082
-JAMES CARVILLE: Absolutely.
-I was talking about it
at the end...

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:53.152
This is a bigger threat
than Al-Qaeda

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:54.686
to this country.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.522
They--
And let me tell you something.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:57.856
They have
the Speaker of the House,

00:05:57.923 --> 00:05:59.425
they got probably--

00:05:59.491 --> 00:06:01.760
At least
two Supreme Court justices,

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.863
maybe more, all right?

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:04.897
Don't kid yourself.

00:06:04.963 --> 00:06:07.933
And people in the press
have no idea

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.336
who this guy is,
how he was formed,

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:11.937
what the threat is,

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:16.876
and this is a fundamental threat
to the United States.

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:17.910
It is a fundamental--

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:19.612
They don't believe
in the Constitution,

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:21.013
they'll tell you that.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.983
Mike Johnson himself says,
"What is democracy,

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:26.552
but two wolves
and a lamb having lunch?"

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:29.021
And that's what they really,
really, really believe.

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:32.058
And to say, "Oh, come on, man.
That's just some crazy shit."

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:34.827
No, no.
They-- They believe that.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:35.828
And they're coming,

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:37.429
and they've
been doing it forever.

00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.333
They're funded. They're funded.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.900
-They're relentless.
-BILL: Yeah.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.937
And, you know,
they probably won't win

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:46.338
for a while, but they might.

00:06:46.438 --> 00:06:47.640
And if they do, it's--

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.141
You blow-- The whole country
blows a gasket.

00:06:49.241 --> 00:06:50.609
You just have to look
at that painting.

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:52.878
I think it's a Kinkade painting,
that a lot of them like,

00:06:52.978 --> 00:06:55.214
where Jesus
is handing the Constitution

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:56.415
-to Thomas Jefferson.
-JAMES: Sure.

00:06:56.848 --> 00:06:58.183
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-BILL: I mean,

00:06:58.617 --> 00:06:59.985
if you can look at that and go,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.154
"Mm. That's the way
it probably happened."

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.856
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:05.992
-I know it-- I know it well.
-That wasn't a photo?

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:07.359
-That wasn't a photo?
-BILL: No, no.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.395
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-BILL: Um.

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.897
"Is the rise of anti-immigration

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.899
Dutch politician
Geert Wilders--"

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:16.435
Ah, I remember interviewing him
for<i> Religulous...</i>

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:18.337
-Yeah. Yeah.
-...way back in 2007.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:20.038
"A warning to the liberals
in America

00:07:20.105 --> 00:07:22.241
that they need to take
our immigration crisis

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.408
more seriously?"

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:25.510
So, if you don't follow
the story,

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.079
Geert Wilders,
he's been running forever

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.047
in Holland.

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.848
Uh. You know,
of course,<i> The New York Times</i>

00:07:29.948 --> 00:07:31.350
calls him a far rightist.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.552
They call all these people,
I mean, Meloni

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:35.521
in Italy is another one.

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.123
Um, Viktor Orbán
is kind of a far rightist

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.359
in Hungary, um, but not--

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.927
I think some of them are just...

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:44.463
Brexit in England
was part of this.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.532
People are feeling
they are not, uh,

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:49.535
welcome, almost,
in their own home

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.170
because of the kind of, uh,

00:07:52.537 --> 00:07:57.610
immigration that these people
are fighting against, so--

00:07:57.676 --> 00:07:59.178
But most of these people
are not far right

00:07:59.245 --> 00:08:01.280
by any way that we would think
of far right in that they--

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:02.782
Like that they're racist.

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:05.584
I actually met with Orbán
in Budapest

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:06.985
and I talked to him
for a little while,

00:08:07.052 --> 00:08:09.455 line:0%
and all he kept saying was,
"You know, I love Hungary.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.857 line:0%
That's all. I love my people.
I love my country."

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.258 line:0%
That's it. I don't know
what accent that was,

00:08:13.325 --> 00:08:15.227 line:0%
-but that basically...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:08:15.293 --> 00:08:18.464
That's a dead-on impression
of him, exact... (HESITATES)

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:20.933
-Can you do his walk?
-DAVE: (CHUCKLES) He kind of--

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:21.934
There's a little bit
of a waddle.

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.203
But all of these guys,
Geert Wilders,

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.906
he wants Holland
to be for the Dutch, right?

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:29.108
-Like, that's what he wants.
-BILL: That's racist.

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:30.943
That's racist. That's what
they would tell you, right?

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.577
No, no. Wait, you meant
that literally or sarcastically?

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:34.046
No, no, no. I'm just-- No.

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:35.214
I don't know what
we're talking about.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.515
-But, um...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:08:36.582 --> 00:08:39.251
I was just gonna say,
Dutch for the Dutch.

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.153
I would amend that if it was me.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.354
Dutch values.

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.422
DAVE: No, Dutch values,
of course.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:44.557
You don't have
to be actually Dutch.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:45.491
You don't have to be White.

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.392
That's what I think
is great about America.

00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:48.661
-It's the idea.
-DAVE: Of course.

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:51.330
As long as you subscribe
to our ideas,

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:52.631
which again, to your point,

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.667
and what I was saying
at the end of the show,

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:57.136
that we're not
a Christian nation.

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:58.237
That's not what it is.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.338
As a country where
we have the First Amendment,

00:09:00.472 --> 00:09:01.807
then everybody
should be welcome.

00:09:01.873 --> 00:09:03.576
No, of course,
it's not about skin color,

00:09:03.642 --> 00:09:04.743
but it is about culture.

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.545
-So, what happens is,
all of these people...
-BILL: Culture matters.

00:09:06.612 --> 00:09:08.914
...whether they're in France
or Belgium

00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.649
or any of the countries
that you just mentioned,

00:09:10.916 --> 00:09:12.184
they're realizing,
"Wow, we've got

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:14.519
literally millions of people
in our borders

00:09:14.753 --> 00:09:17.189
that are chanting for genocide,
and gas the Jews,

00:09:17.255 --> 00:09:18.557
and the rest of it."
And by the way,

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:19.992
it doesn't stop
with the Jews, right?

00:09:20.058 --> 00:09:21.727
I mean, they were
at the Christmas tree

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.762
in Times Square yesterday
or two days ago.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.799
So, people are realizing that,
and they're looking for anybody,

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.533
and for some reason they always
come with crazy hair,

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.836
that will-- that will fix some
of this stuff.

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:32.571
(HESITATES)
I kind of have trouble--

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:33.706
I think your question was,

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:36.709
does the election
in the Netherlands...

00:09:37.043 --> 00:09:38.811
-Is that some part of a warning?
-BILL: A harbinger for--

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.946
Do you want
a short, truthful answer or--

00:09:41.013 --> 00:09:43.616
-BILL: Yes.
-Yes, it does.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.484
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)
-JAMES: Okay? It does.

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:48.888
Said-- Because people--
But understand this.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.790
-People like immigrants, okay?
-DAVE: Right.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:53.892
What they don't like
is disorder.

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.995
And when you become
the disorder party,

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:59.564
whatever it is, you pay a price.

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:03.001
Now, one of the reasons
that we're having this problem,

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:05.971
this is what 3.6 percent
unemployment does for you.

00:10:06.104 --> 00:10:08.407
You think we're the only people
that know that?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.709
Or you think--
And by the way, somebody--

00:10:10.775 --> 00:10:12.677
If you got a woman
that lives in Honduras,

00:10:12.844 --> 00:10:14.613
and she walks
with a ten-year-old

00:10:14.679 --> 00:10:16.515
and a six-year-old
to the Mexican border,

00:10:16.582 --> 00:10:17.883
and wants to come
in this country,

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:20.486
"Come on in, lady.
You motivated person."

00:10:20.553 --> 00:10:22.754
-We need you.
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:24.389
-Period.
-DAVE: No. No.

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:26.625
You can't come.
We have a border.

00:10:26.692 --> 00:10:28.160
We have a border.
We have a country.

00:10:28.226 --> 00:10:30.061
You either have a country
or you don't.

00:10:30.128 --> 00:10:32.564
-I mean--
-Every border had refugees.

00:10:32.697 --> 00:10:34.533
Every border has asylum.

00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:35.934
Yeah, but you can't
just let them walk in.

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:37.102
-I'm sorry.
-That's what the issue is.

00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:38.603
I'm for a six--

00:10:38.737 --> 00:10:40.806
Somebody walks
with two kids 600 miles

00:10:40.872 --> 00:10:41.974
to come in this country,

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:45.077
-"I got a job for you, lady.
Come see me."
-(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:47.146
-BILL: All right--
-Find me one roofer in Florida

00:10:47.213 --> 00:10:48.714
that was born
in the United States.

00:10:48.781 --> 00:10:50.049
-BILL: I got a job too.
-Just find one.

00:10:50.116 --> 00:10:52.084
I got a job and that means
getting out on time.

00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:53.585
Thank you, CNN.
We'll see you next week.

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:55.855
-(AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING)
-Thank you, everybody.

